{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "Recently I have been working on connecting to social media websites via oAuth gems like twitter and koala.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d411ead09f1937c8c827f93d1150d2b232462add856e1dc4fa995716694fda1d.mp3"}, {"text": "I discovered a neat trick for initializing these gems with environment variables so that you don’t have to be passing in the variables every time you want to create a new instance of them.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/82d910cef632fdee7292211051929639ab013d2650cb59b02709a5195c7f66e2.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 0.88], [4, 0.88, 1.16], [5, 1.16, 1.38], [6, 1.38, 1.98], [7, 1.98, 2.24], [8, 2.24, 2.42], [9, 2.42, 2.7], [10, 2.7, 3.08], [11, 3.08, 3.54], [12, 3.54, 4.12], [13, 4.12, 4.24], [14, 4.24, 4.34], [15, 4.34, 4.56], [16, 4.56, 4.66], [17, 4.66, 4.82], [18, 4.82, 4.92], [19, 4.92, 5.2], [20, 5.2, 5.38], [21, 5.38, 5.46], [22, 5.46, 5.82], [23, 5.82, 6.14], [24, 6.14, 6.36], [25, 6.36, 6.52], [26, 6.52, 6.62], [27, 6.62, 6.72], [28, 6.72, 6.92], [29, 6.92, 7.04], [30, 7.04, 7.16], [31, 7.16, 7.46], [32, 7.46, 7.74], [33, 7.74, 7.92]]}, {"text": "For this example, I am going to use the twitter gem.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f4f53c20991bc3a2b485fd353d0f814ca9e8fe4d995e6c3b57c0188cef754272.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.76], [5, 1.18, 1.36], [6, 1.36, 1.6], [7, 1.6, 1.78], [8, 1.78, 1.96], [9, 1.96, 2.18], [10, 2.18, 2.44]]}, {"text": "Out of the box, its initializer looks like this taken from their docs:", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d7736854d65d97cffd888a0328d710e6e89fbc20310a13931b0fb93a9d0a4443.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.42], [3, 0.42, 0.68], [4, 0.86, 0.94], [5, 0.94, 1.52], [6, 1.52, 1.72], [7, 1.72, 1.96], [8, 1.96, 2.22], [9, 2.4, 2.56], [10, 2.56, 2.78], [11, 2.78, 2.94]]}, {"text": "This is pretty clunky if you ask me, especially if you plan on accessing your users data in a variety of different places in your code.", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7011775b8a0b7629a95aa6e314ecf4d4b69a04f2511c3f43c64a28fbb6000b81.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.56], [3, 0.56, 0.96], [4, 0.96, 1.2], [5, 1.2, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.5], [7, 1.5, 1.78], [8, 2.06, 2.74], [9, 2.74, 3.06], [10, 3.06, 3.18], [11, 3.18, 3.4], [12, 3.4, 3.56], [13, 3.56, 4.0], [14, 4.0, 4.28], [16, 4.56, 4.96], [17, 4.96, 5.18], [18, 5.18, 5.26], [19, 5.26, 5.62], [20, 5.62, 5.94], [21, 5.94, 6.28], [22, 6.28, 6.7], [23, 6.7, 6.94], [24, 6.94, 7.06], [25, 7.06, 7.36]]}, {"text": "We can make this more DRY by doing setting the consumer key and consumer secret in an initializer override like this", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c2724b75a767c87295afc24a07c641b6f0fadb6b2a7bc443deb18996bfcf560c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.26], [2, 0.26, 0.4], [3, 0.4, 0.58], [4, 0.58, 0.8], [6, 1.22, 1.42], [7, 1.42, 1.64], [8, 1.64, 1.96], [9, 1.96, 2.16], [10, 2.16, 2.56], [11, 2.56, 2.88], [12, 2.88, 3.14], [13, 3.14, 3.54], [14, 3.54, 4.02], [15, 4.02, 4.3], [16, 4.3, 4.44], [17, 4.44, 5.02], [18, 5.02, 5.42], [19, 5.42, 5.66], [20, 5.66, 5.9]]}, {"text": "```ruby initializers/twitter.rb Twitter::REST::Client.class_eval do def initialize_with_default_settings(options = {}) options[:consumer_key] ||= Rails.application.secrets.fb_app_id options[:consumer_secret] ||= Rails.application.secrets.fb_secret initialize_without_default_settings(options) end", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9efe73a0f2fe70d7103fdc6a8d4f0b9af642fc8e18cf5374aa3bcd6008b250d8.mp3"}, {"text": "alias_method_chain :initialize, :default_settings end", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c0d8e3d635938636f40d23a5bc118e77ac04687fc8783f73ef10d05ae8e04cd3.mp3"}, {"text": "Since the consumer key never changes across calls, this keeps our code that much simpler.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/53c72487fda4bb6361987551c93e7ca59d2b1f45a8542781939dbd964acd427d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.72], [3, 0.72, 0.96], [4, 0.96, 1.2], [5, 1.2, 1.6], [6, 1.6, 1.9], [7, 1.9, 2.4], [8, 2.6, 2.68], [9, 2.68, 2.96], [10, 2.96, 3.16], [11, 3.16, 3.4], [12, 3.4, 3.62], [13, 3.62, 3.8], [14, 3.8, 4.16]]}, {"text": "lowing us to not need to supply the consumer key every time we want to create a new client.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8c0de40033a712ea86c0299a9cda57766671a5d6e91b95a1789de33d449de1ce.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.38, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.72], [3, 0.72, 0.9], [4, 0.9, 1.18], [5, 1.18, 1.34], [6, 1.34, 1.66], [7, 1.66, 1.84], [8, 1.84, 2.28], [9, 2.28, 2.58], [10, 2.58, 2.96], [11, 2.96, 3.2], [12, 3.2, 3.4], [13, 3.4, 3.56], [14, 3.56, 3.74], [15, 3.74, 4.02], [16, 4.02, 4.24], [17, 4.24, 4.38], [18, 4.38, 4.78]]}, {"text": "Now we can do things like this:", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/85fa393d5f68d62f22923fc5d3b4d025cc2d7cd53e8c35fb4f9f6e65ac5cc93d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.46], [3, 0.46, 0.58], [4, 0.58, 0.76], [5, 0.76, 0.98], [6, 0.98, 1.24]]}, {"text": "Since the consumer key never changes across calls, this keeps our code that much simpler.", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/53c72487fda4bb6361987551c93e7ca59d2b1f45a8542781939dbd964acd427d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.72], [3, 0.72, 0.96], [4, 0.96, 1.2], [5, 1.2, 1.6], [6, 1.6, 1.9], [7, 1.9, 2.4], [8, 2.6, 2.68], [9, 2.68, 2.96], [10, 2.96, 3.16], [11, 3.16, 3.4], [12, 3.4, 3.62], [13, 3.62, 3.8], [14, 3.8, 4.16]]}]}